{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuityH7GuH9qWbwfsJpB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Generally, no. `@vitest/runner` is already an internal dependency of `vitest`, and Vitest re-exports the runner APIs you'd normally need. For example, `createTaskCollector`, `getCurrentSuite`, and `setFn` come from `vitest/suite`, and hooks and test functions come from `vitest`. If you also install `@vitest/runner` yourself, its version can drift from the one Vitest uses. You could then end up with two copies of the runner, and state like the current suite or test wouldn't be shared between them. The main case for depending on it directly is building a standalone tool on top of the runner without Vitest itself. If you do that, pin it to exactly the same version as your `vitest`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5810,"cache_read_input_tokens":15764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5810},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a38f0fc-2eca-4587-a2e0-583e88b2fe64","uuid":"80ac7d87-d41f-4a89-bda5-a3623ec6565c","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:15:48.713Z","request_id":"req_011CfuitxzVWNsmdBxyjCMQj"}
